<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	Sign in with Apple is fully implemented (AuthService.signInWithApple()
	+ LoginView's appleButton) but the capability CANNOT be granted yet:
	re-verified 2026-08-08 evening - xcodebuild -allowProvisioningUpdates
	still fails ("Provisioning profile … doesn't include the Sign In with
	Apple capability" / "No Accounts"). Paid Apple Developer Program
	membership + Apple ID signed into Xcode Accounts is required.

	When that lands, flip it on:
	  1. Add here:
	     <key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	     <array><string>Default</string></array>
	  2. Set LoginView.appleSignInEnabled = true
	  3. Enable the Apple provider in Firebase console → Authentication
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
